{"action":"","actor":"","alternative_quotes":["(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or","(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:

(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;

(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or

(iii) An off-site designated facility."],"choice_text":"A generator accumulating in excess of satellite limits must choose either to comply within three consecutive calendar days with central accumulation area requirements, or to remove the excess within three consecutive calendar days to one of three locations: a central accumulation area, an on-site permitted/permit-by-rule facility, or an off-site designated facility.","claimants":[],"concepts":[],"effective_periods":[],"jurisdiction":"","kind":"requirement","logic_text":"","modality":"must","object":"","scope_text":"As a condition for exemption for satellite accumulation under rule 3745-52-15.","summary":"As a condition for exemption for satellite accumulation, a generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-15 at or near any point of generation shall do either of the following: (a) within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or (b) remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either (i) a central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, (ii) an on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility, or (iii) an off-site designated facility.","typed_values":[]}
